MewStage vendor patch text/0001 (third_party/NOTICE): a paragraph's LetterSpacing widened the layout's columns but a
backend run was still drawn whole, at the font's own advances, so letter-spaced text drew unspaced. A letter-spaced
text run is now drawn one grapheme at a time at its column (paint spans per grapheme, decorations over the run).
Unspaced text is unchanged. A grapheme's run box is at least its own measured advance: a negative kerning pair
narrows the column, and a backend that rasterizes a run into its box plus the ink overhang it measures from the
glyphs' own advances (MewVG Win32 / X11, GDI, Direct2D) cut the glyph at the kerned column.

